{
  "storyId": "B-e37e",
  "name": "authority-runner-jobs-sse-client",
  "title": "Make Authority runner prefer job-available SSE with safe polling fallback",
  "description": "Lattice CLI authority runner currently relies on register/heartbeat/claim polling behavior. Once Lattice Authority Server upgrades /v1/runners/{runnerId}/jobs/stream from a snapshot to a long-lived job-available SSE stream, the CLI should consume that stream to reduce idle waiting while preserving claim authority, signed runner identity, and polling fallback when SSE is unavailable or still snapshot-only.",
